		<title>Greyparrot Secures $27 Million in Series B Funding To Scale AI Waste Intelligence Platform</title>
		<link>https://ventureburn.com/greyparrot-secures-27-million-series-b-ai-waste-intelligence/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Ekemini]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:42:33 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Startup]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Venture Capital]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI hardware]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Analyzers]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[artificial intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Greyparrot]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://ventureburn.com/?p=203798</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Among the industries unaffected by artificial intelligence, the waste industry has crept under the radar. Greyparrot secures $27 million in a Series B round to replace the waste industry with</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/greyparrot-secures-27-million-series-b-ai-waste-intelligence/" data-wpel-link="internal">Greyparrot Secures $27 Million in Series B Funding To Scale AI Waste Intelligence Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Among the industries unaffected by artificial intelligence, the waste industry has crept under the radar. Greyparrot secures $27 million in a </span><a href="https://www.greyparrot.ai/series-b" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">Series B round</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> to replace the waste industry with data. The London-based startup uses artificial intelligence to track and identify discarded items inside recycling facilities. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The investment is a response to the increasing pressure that is being put on sorting facilities to increase their recovery rates and comply with strict sustainability requirements. Greyparrot will use the new funds to expand its team, upgrade hardware and scale the AI waste intelligence platform to North America and Europe. </span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Scaling AI Intelligence Across Global Plants</span></h2>
<div id="attachment_203800" style="width: 760px" class="wp-caption aligncenter"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203800" class="size-full wp-image-203800" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Greyparrot-Analyzer-1200x800_courtesyGreyparrot-750x500-1.jpg" alt="Greyparrot&apos;s Analyzer system collects data from MRF streams that could help inform EPR policy and recover overlooked revenue." width="750" height="500" /><p id="caption-attachment-203800" class="wp-caption-text">Greyparrot Analyzer</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Recycling centers process millions of tons of material every day, but operators rarely know what is actually moving through their lines. Greyparrot changes that by mounting camera units called Analyzers above conveyor belts. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These units use computer vision to scan items in real time. They spot plastics, metals, paper, and specific brand packaging as materials move past. By bringing artificial intelligence into physical processing plants, the system replaces slow, imprecise manual sampling with automated analytical reporting. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding will help Greyparrot install more units across major markets. Its client list already includes waste giants like Veolia, WM, and Biffa, alongside consumer brands such as Unilever and L’Oréal.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/hush-security-raises-30m-ai-agent-governance-gap/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Hush Security Raises $30M for Governance AI Agents</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Greyparrot Surpasses One Trillion Waste Detections</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Greyparrot recently hit a massive milestone by surpassing one trillion waste detections. That dataset gives recyclers deep insight into what they throw away. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">So far, 17.4 billion PET plastic bottles and 4.2 billion aluminum objects have been recognized by the system. Aluminum can be recycled to reduce up to 95% of energy required to produce new metal. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">It is eco-friendly and economical to locate those items before they end up in landfills. With AI, facilities can achieve a more comprehensive 100x coverage of waste, which covers less than 0.1 percent of waste without AI.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">New government rules are forcing brands and recyclers to monitor their environmental footprint. In the United States, seven states have passed Extended Producer Responsibility laws for packaging. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These rules require companies to pay for the end-of-life processing of their products and report precise recycling metrics. Greyparrot provides the verified data needed to meet these strict compliance standards.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates:</i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/multiverse-computing-raises-570-million-for-expansion/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i> Multiverse Computing Raises $570M for Global Expansion</i></b></a></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400">Turning Recovered Material Into Revenue</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Missing recyclable material costs money. Greyparrot estimates its platform has already spotted $2.5 billion in recoverable material value across facility networks. Facilities using the system report operational efficiency gains between 10 and 30 percent. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">For one site, this can equate to over $2 million per year in savings. In this way, managers can change sorting machines on the go and recover valuable products before they lose them due to the poor efficiency. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Co-founder Ambarish Mitra said it was a blind spot that has been there for decades. If they can measure the materials accurately then they can trade the materials; they can trade the recycled materials with a certainty and with a confidence that they can do the job in a reliable way.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">CEO Mikela Druckman highlighted that data is the core infrastructure required to unlock circular economy goals. With new funding in place, the company is set to turn waste data into standard industrial infrastructure.</span></p>
<p><b><i>More Updates: </i></b><a href="https://ventureburn.com/ropedia-raises-30m-pre-a-funding-scale-physical-ai-infrastructure/" data-wpel-link="internal"><b><i>Ropedia Raises $30M To Scale Physical AI Data Infrastructure</i></b></a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/greyparrot-secures-27-million-series-b-ai-waste-intelligence/" data-wpel-link="internal">Greyparrot Secures $27 Million in Series B Funding To Scale AI Waste Intelligence Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
