					<description><![CDATA[<p>ProphetX Raises $35M To Scale Prediction Market Platform ProphetX has raised a $35 million round in order to boost its federally regulated sports betting and prediction market. The company intends</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/prophetx-raises-35m-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">ProphetX Raises $35M to Expand Federally Regulated Sports Prediction Market</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>ProphetX Raises $35M To Scale Prediction Market Platform</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">ProphetX has raised a $35 million round in order to boost its federally regulated sports betting and prediction market. The company intends to add value to the product, expand market liquidity and reinforce business relationships that are currently supporting their increasing B2B model.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The round was headed by Parlay Capital and Data Point Capital, but the round also attracted investment from FDJ Ventures, Greenwave Ventures, Connexa Capital, Impellent Ventures, the Operating Group, Sharp Alpha Advisors and a number of proprietary trading firms. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">ProphetX was initially founded in 2018 and allows users to trade contracts on sporting events in a regulated exchange. The vision of the company is to create a transparent betting environment enabling private traders and institutional traders alike to access a trading platform governed by the regulated financial world.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding To Drive Product Innovation And B2B Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">ProphetX intends to put the new financing into the scaling up of its proprietary technological platform, in increasing liquidity in different markets and for creating new product categories targeting retail consumers and B2B customers. The funding is to also be used to finance business growth.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Rather than relying solely on direct consumer activity, ProphetX plans to offer its exchange infrastructure to business partners, enabling them to integrate regulated </span><a href="https://www.investopedia.com/terms/p/prediction-market.asp" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">prediction markets</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> into their own products and services.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company intends to strengthen its proprietary Request for Quote (RFQ) Parlay Mechanism, which enables users to build and price multi-event contracts directly with counterparties. The mechanism is designed to deliver greater pricing transparency, flexibility, and efficiency.</span></p>
<h2><b>Regulated Exchange Offers Alternative To Traditional Sportsbooks</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_203781" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-203781" class="size-full wp-image-203781" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/ProphetX-3.png" alt="Illustration of a regulated sports prediction exchange showing peer-to-peer betting markets, transparent pricing, liquidity flows, and digital trading infrastructure." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-203781" class="wp-caption-text">Regulated prediction markets are introducing a new approach to sports trading by combining peer-to-peer exchanges, transparent pricing, and financial market-style infrastructure to improve liquidity and user participation. Source: Created by Ventureburn.</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Whereas traditional online bookmakers stand as the opposing side to every bet placed, ProphetX acts as a peer-to-peer exchange for users to place bets against each other. ProphetX takes its commissions at a low fixed transparent fee for each bet taken rather than making them offset its losing side of bets with customers&#8217; wins.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This exchange model allows participants to determine market prices collectively while improving price discovery and liquidity. It also aligns the platform more closely with financial exchanges than traditional betting operators.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company reported encouraging early growth following its transition from a sweepstakes platform to a federally regulated prediction market. Within the first month of operating under its new regulatory framework, ProphetX recorded a 50% increase in both active users and assets held on the platform.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/enigma-raises-71m-to-advance-physical-ai-for-robotics/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Enigma Raises $71M to Advance Physical AI for Robotics</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Investors Back Long-Term Growth In Event Markets</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Investors believe ProphetX is well positioned to benefit from the growing convergence between financial markets and event-based trading. The participation of venture capital firms alongside proprietary trading companies reflects increasing institutional interest in regulated prediction markets as a new asset class.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief Executive Officer Dean Sisun said the latest financing provides the resources needed to meet rising demand from consumers and institutions. He noted that prediction markets are becoming a permanent part of the American financial landscape, with ProphetX aiming to establish itself as a leading platform in the sector.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Parlay Capital described ProphetX as building infrastructure that could shape how both retail users and institutional investors participate in sports prediction markets. Data Point Capital also highlighted the company&#8217;s regulatory position and technology platform as important advantages in an evolving market.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/prophetx-raises-35m-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">ProphetX Raises $35M to Expand Federally Regulated Sports Prediction Market</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
